---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlueprintCard from '../components/BlueprintCard.astro';
import RunReplay from '../islands/RunReplay';
import { BLUEPRINTS } from '../data/blueprints';
import '../styles/playground.css';

const repo = 'https://github.com/plnt-work/plnt';
const featured = BLUEPRINTS.filter((b) => b.status === 'ships').slice(0, 6);

const enforced = [
  {
    title: 'A private workspace per session',
    body: 'Every session works on its own copy of the folder or repo. Agents read and change the copy; the source is never touched.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Tools by policy, not by prompt',
    body: 'Read-only mode strips write_file and execute before the agent ever sees them. The public playground runs that way.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Look before you answer',
    body: 'A bundle can require a tool. An answer the model gives before reading a file is withheld, not sent.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Budgets and a kill switch',
    body: 'Token, wall-clock and step limits per agent, a loop detector, and a kill that stops the running agents and skips the rest.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Everything on the record',
    body: 'The parent’s decision and reason, each agent’s spec, every model call, tool call and file, usage per agent. Streamed live, folded into a transcript.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Any model, per tenant',
    body: 'Gemini, OpenAI, or a local Ollama, vLLM or llama.cpp box. Chosen per tenant, checked with plnt models doctor before you rely on it.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="plnt: a task in, micro-agents out"
  description="Open-source runtime where a parent agent takes a task on your repo, decides which micro-agents to spawn, runs them isolated, and merges the result. Every step visible."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow accent">Open source · Apache-2.0 · runtime for micro-agents</div>
      <h1>A task in. Micro-agents out.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        plnt runs a <b>parent</b> that reads a task on your repository, decides which agents to
        create and what each should do, runs them in isolation on a private copy of the
        workspace, and merges the result into one reply. The decision, each agent’s spec, every
        file it read and every model call are on the record, live.
      </p>
      <div class="ctas">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/playground">Try it on a demo repo</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
        <a class="btn" href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <div class="install">
        <pre><code is:raw><span class="c"># pre-alpha: install from source</span>
pip install "git+https://github.com/plnt-work/plnt"
plnt dev code-reviewer --workspace .      <span class="c"># API + console on 127.0.0.1:8787</span>
<span class="c"># open http://127.0.0.1:8787/console → Sessions → New session</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">How a run works</span>
      <h2>One task, one parent, as many agents as it takes.</h2>
      <div class="how">
        <div class="how-step">
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <h3>You give a task</h3>
          <p>“Audit <code>app/store.py</code> for bugs and write tests for it.” On a workspace: a demo repo, a folder, or a git URL.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="how-step">
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <h3>The parent decides</h3>
          <p>One structured model call: answer, ask, or spawn. For each agent: which bundle, an intent in your words, what it depends on. Recorded with its reason.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="how-step">
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <h3>Agents run isolated</h3>
          <p>Independent agents run in parallel; dependent ones wait and get the upstream results. Each has its own tools, budget and guardrails on the session’s copy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="how-step">
          <span class="num">04</span>
          <h3>One reply, full trace</h3>
          <p>The parent merges the answers. The transcript keeps the plan, every agent’s spec, steps, files and tokens. Watch it in the console or the playground.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">A real run, replayed</span>
      <h2>What you see while it works.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        Recorded from the playground on the <code>notes-api</code> demo workspace, with the events
        exactly as the runtime streamed them. Open the playground to run your own.
      </p>
      <RunReplay client:visible />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Blueprints</span>
      <h2>What people point it at.</h2>
      <p class="sub">The four shipped bundles cover the coding tasks. Everything else is a bundle you write, or a role the parent invents.</p>
      <div class="bp-grid">
        {featured.map((bp) => <BlueprintCard bp={bp} />)}
      </div>
      <p class="more"><a href="/use-cases">All use cases →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">What the runtime enforces</span>
      <h2>Not left to each agent to get right.</h2>
      <div class="grid three">
        {enforced.map((f) => (
          <div class="card">
            <h3>{f.title}</h3>
            <p>{f.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Local models</span>
      <h2>Checked before you rely on them.</h2>
      <p class="sub">
        <code>plnt models doctor</code> checks what an agent needs: the server is up, the model is
        pulled, it calls tools, it returns JSON, the context window fits. Failures come with the fix.
      </p>
      <div class="grid two">
        <pre><code is:raw>$ plnt models doctor
qwen2.5:7b  ollama · http://127.0.0.1:11434 · local
  ✓ reachable       http://127.0.0.1:11434
  ✓ model present   qwen2.5:7b
  ✓ context window  requesting 8192 of 32768 tokens
  ✓ tool calling    native; called get_weather(city='Paris')
  ✓ JSON output     got {'answer': 42}</code></pre>
        <pre><code is:raw>$ plnt run code-reviewer "find bugs" --workspace .
✗ cannot reach Ollama at http://127.0.0.1:11434
  fix: start it with `ollama serve` (or fix PLNT_LOCAL_URL)

<span class="c"># no silent fallback to a canned answer: a model</span>
<span class="c"># failure is reported as a failure, with the fix.</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Status</span>
      <p class="status">
        Pre-alpha (0.1). The parent, the four developer bundles, workspaces, the multi-tenant API,
        the console and the playground are built and tested in CI, including against a real local
        model. Bundle tool code runs inside the server process, so only install bundles you
        trust; sandboxed tools, nested parents and a hosted registry are on the
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/ROADMAP.md`}>roadmap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
